; The record types Flow's Memory keeps that Operation names: how a launch
; request settled, kept beside its attempt so LaunchStatus and
; Observe.Launch answer it without running the launch again, and a
; replacement under way, the successor's launch request and the predecessor
; it reaps. SeatBirth is the seat a restart bound: the route it runs in and
; the birth of its harness process, kept after the restart's record goes, so
; an event of the seat it replaced is told from the seat's own.

Memory
[ signal_flow:[ LaunchRequestId StartRejection ReplaceRejection FlowId HerdrRoute Process NativeSessionId TranscriptPath BackgroundWork NativePrompt ]
  flow_nexus:[ LaunchedRecord ReplacedRecord ] ]
[ LaunchOutcome.[ Started.LaunchedRecord
                  Replaced.ReplacedRecord
                  StartRejected.StartRejection
                  ReplaceRejected.ReplaceRejection ]
  Replacement.{ LaunchRequestId Predecessor.String }
  SeatBirth.{ FlowId HerdrRoute Process }
  ; A recorded Stop holds its correlation and background-work metadata.
  RecordedStop.{ Option<NativeSessionId> Option<TranscriptPath> BackgroundWork }
  ; Harness metadata in report order, independent of transient transport.
  RecordedHarnessEvent.[ Started.Option<NativeSessionId>
                         ToolUsed.String
                         Stopped.RecordedStop
                         PromptSubmitted.NativePrompt
                         Ended.Option<NativeSessionId>
                         Cleared.Option<NativeSessionId> ]
  ; One flow's durable metadata; its original key is preserved exactly.
  FlowEvents.{ FlowId Vector<RecordedHarnessEvent> } ]
